      "text": [
        " : قُلْتُ لَهُ إِنَّ فِي بَلَدِنَا رُبَّمَا أُوصِيَ بِالْمَالِ، لآِلِ مُحَمَّدٍ فَيَأْتُونِّي بِهِ فَأَكْرَهُ أَنْ أَحْمِلَهُ إِلَيْكَ حَتَّى أَسْتَأْمِرَكَ فَقَالَ \"لاَ تَأْتِنِي بِهِ وَ لاَ تَعَرَّضْ لَهُ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5558 - Ali ibn Mahziyar narrated from Ahmad ibn Hamzah, who said:\nI said to Imam (as): 'In our town, sometimes people bequeath wealth to the family of Muhammad (sw), and they bring it to me. However, I hesitate to deliver it to you until I seek your permission.'\nImam (as) replied: \"Do not bring it to me, and do not involve yourself with it.\""
        ]
      }
